# A1-P02 — The Wrong Weapon. Source: Production Master 2.1, lines 1221–1311.
# Scene: scenes/chapter1/elara_meeting.tscn. The combat tutorial happens only
# when danger can't be avoided: the slime follows if you back off and attacks
# if you wait.
# Every branch keeps Elara with Kaelen. The legacy flags ch1_elara_trusted and
# ch1_elara_cautious are what GameManager.has_elara() reads.

~ start
Kaelen: ...Why do I have a sword?
Kaelen: I don't own a sword.
Kaelen: I own a sword.
do slime_appears

~ after_slime
Kaelen: That... wasn't blood.
???: Were you hoping it would be?
do elara_enters
Elara: Hands where I can see them.
Kaelen: One of them's holding a sword.
Elara: Then put that one down first.
Kaelen: Okay. Putting it down. Slowly.
do kaelen_lowers_sword
Elara: Name?
Kaelen: Kaelen.
Elara: From where?
Kaelen: Flight 707.
Elara: Is that a place?
Kaelen: It's a plane. It's— it flies. It's a big metal thing that flies.
# She looks at him the way you'd look at someone describing a dragon made of spoons.
Kaelen: You didn't see anything fall today? Out of the sky?
Elara: You.
Kaelen: Anyone else? Smoke, wreckage, people?
Elara: No.
Elara: Were there supposed to be?
Kaelen: ...A lot.
do elara_lowers_bow
Elara: Then let's talk somewhere the road isn't trying to eat us.
? Kaelen (Internal): How much do I tell her?
- I was on a flight. Something happened, I woke up here, and everyone else is gone. => trust
- There were people with me. I need to find them before I explain the rest. => cautious
- You first. Where am I? Then I'll tell you how impossible this is. => deflect

~ trust
set elara_first_truth
set ch1_elara_trusted
do trust elara 10
Elara: You remember them.
Kaelen: Enough.
Elara: Good. Hold on to that.
Kaelen: Why is that good?
Elara: People who come out of bad places usually come out remembering less.
=> after

~ cautious
set elara_first_cautious
set ch1_elara_cautious
Elara: You remember enough to be careful.
Kaelen: I remember enough to know I should be looking.
Elara: Then we want the same thing. For now.
=> after

~ deflect
set elara_first_deflect
set ch1_elara_cautious
Elara: Oakhaven Reach.
Kaelen: Is that a country?
Elara: A region.
Kaelen: Of which country? Which— where?
Elara: Aethelgard.
Kaelen (Internal): Nothing. It's not a word I know. It's not even close to one.
=> after

~ after
set elara_met
Elara: You came out of the crater, stranger.
Kaelen: I guess I did.
Elara: People don't come out of the crater.
Kaelen: Great. Today's going great.
Elara: Oakhaven keeps road records. Travellers, strangers... things that fall out of places they shouldn't.
Kaelen: That happens often enough to need records?
Elara: Often enough that Bran complains about the paperwork.
do kaelen_reaches_for_sword
do elara_raises_bow
Kaelen: Right. Sorry. Leaving that there.
Elara: Walk ahead of me, where I can see you.
Kaelen: Very trusting.
Elara: Very practical.
do objective Reach Oakhaven. Follow the first lead on the missing passengers.
